44
00:03:18,795 --> 00:03:21,722
Rym: Like, it actually looks like modem-style data packets.

45
00:03:22,303 --> 00:03:41,810
Rym: It's periodic, it recurs at about two hertz, it rotates through about five distinct sets of tones that I can see, and I even, I was able to isolate several of these notes and find that there are, in fact, four or five harmonic peaks that move in a pattern in the audio.

46
00:03:42,311 --> 00:04:05,229
Rym: The amplitude of this is proportional to the amplitude of the audio itself, so I since recorded multiple hockey games in their entirety, and dug deeper, and I also found some other sources, and I'm going to continue to share my analysis of this in the forum as I figure out what the fuck's going on, but it is absolutely real, you can see it in the audio, and I'm super annoyed by it.

47
00:04:05,931 --> 00:04:12,521
